has spent the last four months tending  to his farms hoping to profit from his  harvests but when torrential rains and  floods hit sudan's jazeera state much of  his land was submerged destroying the  crops have about 300 acres that were  farmed this season the rains and floods  have covered about 300 acres all what is  completely destroyed is a complete  disaster  some are trying to drain the water but  as a farmer this summer season has been  a complete loss  heavy rains and floods have affected  more than 90 000 acres in jazeera state  home to the largest governmental  agricultural project in sudan more than  130 000 farmers grow crops such as corn  and cotton for the country and  international markets but rain and  floods have affected that as well as the  economy of the state authorities say  hundreds of thousands of dollars worth  of produce have been lost  as farmers this is a loss for us this  season i'll not be having anything to  sell  the corn and anything else i planted is  gone i've lost more than a million  chinese pounds because of the flooding  and farmers income are not the only  concern the flooding of farmlands comes  at a critical time for sudan the united  nations says a third of the people in  the country or about 15 million are  already struggling to get enough food  and with flood waters covering tens of  thousands of acres that number may rise  even further  jazeera is known as the bread basket of  sudam supplying half of the crops it  needs any disruption in that supply  could raise market prices in a country  where more than half of the people live  in poverty authorities say they've put  plans in place to reduce the impact of  floods if it has a museum  we will split up the farming cycles to  make up for the losses the farmers have  incurred the amount of lands farmers  plant on during the winter season will  be increased based on the area of land  that has been destroyed by the reins  but farmers like  fear their lands may not recover in time  for the coming season and they may  suffer more economic losses  heber morgan al jazeera jazeera state
 

